rows.en:
The girls' restroom on the east side of the first floor.
That's the one.
Inside that restroom there's a grimy, blackish stain.{p}

With an aura, you usually get a kind of premonition as you get close.
Like, oh, there's one around here.
The stronger the aura, the stronger you feel it.{p}

That's what I did, too.
I just couldn't leave a girl who looked about to cry, after all.
To be safe, we decided to go in and see the stain for ourselves.{p}

The door opened, and Ms. Hida came in.
She was holding a towel.
Something was wrapped up in it.{p}

Apparently, when one of her gang went to visit Saijo in the hospital, her whole face was covered in a horrible stain.
They say that stain looked exactly like the one in the restroom.
No treatment could get rid of the stain on Saijo's face, and after that she didn't want to see anyone, and then she vanished without a trace.{p}

Ms. Hida smiled at us, relieved, maybe.
"I see. Thank you, everyone.
...To tell you the truth, the girl who was made to lick that restroom stain was me."{p}

When I asked the other girls, they said her name was Tomita, and that she was always bragging about having a sixth sense.
But no matter how long we waited, Tomita didn't come out.
We got nervous and peeked inside the restroom.{p}

Tomita went limp and passed out.
...In other words, pathetically enough, I got saved by a girl.
The teachers noticed the commotion, came running, and took Tomita away.{p}
